  "title": "The Audience-Powered Curtain",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "cooperation",
  "premise": "A puppet crew wants to reveal a show, but the curtain is tied to several short ropes scattered through the seats. Instead of one frantic operator chasing every rope, the crew invites each seated figure to hold a section and raise it together on a visible count.",
  "hook": "The show starts when all of us lift.",
  "visible_action": "Operator runs between rope ends; ropes droop; seated figures take one each; count cards flip; curtain rises evenly.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Distributing a task can make its timing manageable.",
  "gate": "Fictional lightweight puppet curtain; not a real rigging or crowd-participation safety design.",
